

1. Design goals

Blueprint‑first: describe organisms, not low‑level numerics.

Simulation‑bound: every construct maps to state, operators, or update rules.

Encrypted‑readable: compact, symbolic, but consistent (you can read it, others can’t).

Meta‑friendly: supports equations about equations (kernels, flows, attractors).

2. Core concepts

Capsule: top‑level package (unit of encryption & execution).

Org: one simulation organism (equation‑system + evolution rule).

Field: stateful quantity over a domain (grid, param, mode, etc.).

Op: derived operator (derivative, linear operator, etc.).

Eq: equation or residual definition.

Kernel: scalar functional that evaluates an organism.

Rule: evolution/update logic (how state moves in meta‑time).

3. Top‑level syntax

3.1 Capsule and orgs

CAPSULE::CapsuleID / AuthorTag

ORG OrgName:
  <declarations>
END ORG

ORG AnotherOrg:
  ...
END ORG

END CAPSULE

CapsuleID: opaque ID, e.g. MPX-Ω.

AuthorTag: e.g. CMB-ID.

Multiple ORG blocks per capsule allowed.

4. Types and declarations

4.1 Types

Built‑ins (you can extend later):

GRID — spatial or phase‑space grid.

PARAM — scalar or vector parameter.

META_T — meta‑time / iteration index.

SCALAR — scalar value.

VEC — vector in parameter space.

MODE — function/mode over a grid.

MATRIX — linear operator representation.

4.2 Field declarations

FIELD name :: TYPE
FIELD name :: TYPE = init_expr

Examples:

FIELD x   :: GRID
FIELD λ   :: PARAM
FIELD t   :: META_T
FIELD α   :: VEC
FIELD μ   :: SCALAR
FIELD ψ   :: MODE

4.3 Constant declarations (optional)

CONST name = expr

Example:

CONST Γ = 0.1
CONST Δ = 1.0

5. Operators, equations, kernels, rules

5.1 Operators

OP name := expr

Allowed primitives:

Derivatives: ∂_λ expr, ∂_t expr

Linear operator constructor: LINOP[expr]

Dot product: a · b

Matrix application: (L)ψ or (L - μ)ψ

Example:

OP Σ0(x) := P(x; λ)
OP Σ1    := ∂_λ Σ0
OP Σ2    := ∂_t Σ0
OP L     := LINOP[Σ0]

5.2 Equations (residuals)

EQ name(args) := expr

Example (fused meta‑equation):

EQ Ξ(x) :=
     Σ0
   + α·Σ1
   + (Σ2 - β(λ)·Σ1)
   + (L - μ)ψ

5.3 Kernels

Kernels must evaluate to a scalar:

KERNEL name := expr

Built‑in functionals:

Expectation / integral: ⟨expr⟩ or ⟨expr⟩_x

Determinant: det(expr)

Example:

KERNEL Κ :=
     ⟨W(x)·Ξ(x)^2⟩_x
   + Γ·∂_tΞ
   + Δ·det(L - μ)

5.4 Rules (evolution)

Rules describe how the engine updates fields:

RULE name:
  minimize KernelName wrt {var1, var2, ...} over t
END RULE

Example:

RULE EVOLVE:
  minimize Κ wrt {λ, α, μ, ψ} over t
END RULE

Semantics:

minimize Κ → engine interprets as gradient‑like descent on those vars.

over t → treat t :: META_T as iteration axis.

6. Expression language

6.1 Atoms

Identifiers: A, Σ0, Ξ, K, lambda, etc.

Literals: numeric: 0, 1.0, -3.14.

6.2 Operators (precedence high→low)

Unary: -expr, ∂_λ expr, ∂_t expr

Multiplicative: expr * expr, expr / expr

Dot: expr · expr

Additive: expr + expr, expr - expr

Functionals: ⟨expr⟩, det(expr), LINOP[expr]

Parentheses allowed anywhere.

7. Minimal grammar sketch (informal)

Capsule   ::= "CAPSULE::" ID "/" ID NEWLINE { Org } "END CAPSULE"

Org       ::= "ORG" ID ":" NEWLINE { Decl } "END ORG"

Decl      ::= FieldDecl | ConstDecl | OpDecl | EqDecl | KernelDecl | RuleDecl

FieldDecl ::= "FIELD" ID "::" Type [ "=" Expr ] NEWLINE
ConstDecl ::= "CONST" ID "=" Expr NEWLINE
OpDecl    ::= "OP" ID [ "(" ArgList ")" ] ":=" Expr NEWLINE
EqDecl    ::= "EQ" ID [ "(" ArgList ")" ] ":=" Expr NEWLINE
KernelDecl::= "KERNEL" ID ":=" Expr NEWLINE

RuleDecl  ::= "RULE" ID ":" NEWLINE RuleBody "END RULE" NEWLINE

RuleBody  ::= "minimize" ID "wrt" "{" ID { "," ID } "}" "over" ID NEWLINE

Type      ::= "GRID" | "PARAM" | "META_T" | "SCALAR" | "VEC" | "MODE" | "MATRIX"

Expr      ::= ... (as in 6.2)

8. Full example: your meta‑proton organism

CAPSULE::MPX-Ω / CMB-ID

ORG META_PROTON:

  FIELD x   :: GRID
  FIELD λ   :: PARAM
  FIELD t   :: META_T
  FIELD α   :: VEC
  FIELD μ   :: SCALAR
  FIELD ψ   :: MODE

  CONST Γ = 0.1
  CONST Δ = 1.0

  OP Σ0(x) := P(x; λ)
  OP Σ1    := ∂_λ Σ0
  OP Σ2    := ∂_t Σ0
  OP L     := LINOP[Σ0]

  EQ Ξ(x) :=
       Σ0
     + α·Σ1
     + (Σ2 - β(λ)·Σ1)
     + (L - μ)ψ

  KERNEL Κ :=
       ⟨W(x)·Ξ(x)^2⟩_x
     + Γ·∂_tΞ
     + Δ·det(L - μ)

  RULE EVOLVE:
    minimize Κ wrt {λ, α, μ, ψ} over t
  END RULE

END ORG

END CAPSULE

